The signs of the Zodiac are different from the constellations in which
the sun moves.

The signs are fixed to locations that are 2,000 years out of date.
Because of the precession of the equinoxes, the constellations have
moved.

Right now, for example, the sun is in Libra; that is not its sign.
At the beginning of December, the sun will be in Ophiuchus, which is
not even a traditional sign.

